markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>The Reactive Logic Project: Goals and Milestones</h1>

<p>This is the unit's capstone. Everything from web app structure through loops and conditionals comes together here: students plan, build, and reflect on an interactive app of their own design over five class days.</p>

---

<h2>Sample Project</h2>
<p>Remember the project from the beginning of the module. Now it's time to dive in.</p>
<p><em>Click the ingredients and see what happens.</em></p>

<div style="width:100%; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; margin:20px 0;">
  <iframe src="https://amandadennard-dotcom.github.io/Unit5AIF2/trail-mix-badge-builder-v2.html" width="100%" height="720" style="border:none;" title="Trail Mix Badge Builder sample project"></iframe>
</div>

<h2>Project Goals</h2>

<p style="margin: 0 0 8px 0;">• Plan and model the logic for an interactive app that produces different outcomes based on user input</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 8px 0;">• Use JavaScript conditionals, logical operators, and variables to manage app behavior and display</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 8px 0;">• Organize and structure code with functions and event-driven design</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• Reflect on how AI tools and their own creative decisions shaped the process</p>

<h2 style="text-align:center; color:#4C42CF; margin-bottom:8px;">Project Roadmap</h2>

<p style="text-align:center; margin-top:0;">Follow the four milestones from planning through final reflection.</p>

<div style="width:100%; overflow-x:auto; margin:28px 0; padding-bottom:10px;">

  <div role="list" aria-label="Four project milestones" style="position:relative; display:flex; align-items:stretch; gap:18px; min-width:820px; padding:24px 12px 12px 12px; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">

<!-- Road -->
